window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Willow: In the past three weeks, I’ve gone from a boring adjunct college professor to seeing my own ghostly doppelgänger around every corner. I’m apparently a witch. Thanks, Universe. A little heads up would have been nice. Now, a secret government organization is trying to force me to wield my power for their own dark desires. Just as they’re about to bring the pain, I’m saved by an honest-to-God—yes, that God—angel. He smells nice. His voice is like spun gold. And when he holds me? I’m ashamed to admit…I swoon. But I can’t trust anyone—not even a celestial. I’m so screwed. Because somewhere between running for my life and running from him, I’ve fallen in love with my angel protector—and soon, he’ll have to go back home. </p> <p>Gabriel: I am the Archangel Gabriel. Bringer of Justice, Revealer of Truth, and the Interpreter of the Almighty’s plan. I came to earth to help a demon, but the experience turned my celestial existence upside down. As it turns out, this realm is not all sunshine and rainbows. More like a swirling vortex of chaos. I have not seen a single harp. Wings are actively frowned upon. As are robes, for that matter. But humans—and their emotions—are fascinating. One human in particular. Willow Saunders. She’s in trouble. I alone can protect her. And I will.</p>"; 
